The attached image is relevant. The attached image, corresponding to Figure 7D in the PDF, presents a Western blot analysis confirming the secretion of active IL-1β by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs) treated with Nano-11, particularly after LPS priming. The blot shows bands at approximately 17 kD in the supernatant, indicative of the active form of IL-1β, which is distinct from the biologically inactive 31 kD pro-IL-1β. This verifies that Nano-11, especially when combined with LPS, induces the processing and release of active IL-1β, a crucial pro-inflammatory cytokine, as discussed in Section 3.4 of the article.